        "note": "D-16-5 fixes the window: 256 by 256 cells at 1,000 cm, 2.56 km square, offset to 20,000 m so its frame cannot touch the lot's or the harness's. The entry zones are sixteen cells deep on each short side. The key spots are where the ground decides something: the ford, the crossroads, the two compounds. The waypoint graph is the two roads and four spurs, the smallest on which Patrol's route is not a straight line. VERSION 2 (16b cut F.4) moves the muster onto the ford: version 1 mustered on rows 118 to 130, and the river (columns 62 to 66) stopped a tank at deep water 550 m out. The ford is rows 92 to 102; slot 1 stands on the east-west road at row 97 and slots 2 to 4 at 95, 99 and 93, so every tank drives straight across. The muster nodes moved to row 105. VERSION 3 (16b cut Z.3) adds slots 5 and 6 a side: row 101 in the muster column and row 94 one column behind it, both inside the ford's rows 92 to 102, a clear cell from every other slot and on no other slot's straight road east or west."
